      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Mg toxicity:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " respiratory depression, acute renal failure, rarely pulmonary edema; monitor for facial edema, ↓DTRs and respiratory depression, and check Mg levels during infusion; DTRs ↓ once Mg > 4 mEq/L and may be absent at 10 mEq/L (respiratory paralysis risk); keep an injectable calcium salt on hand to counteract it."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
